tags: []
date: 2026-04-13T00:00:00-04:00
---

The sewers beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] are made to carry the city's waste and are not built to be defended; there are many ways in and out. A manhole in the open-air market of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] drops onto a pumping floor that feeds into the sewer proper, and the [[Anti-Zorbon Taskforce|Anti-Zorbon Taskforce]] kept a hideout further along. There is also a public exit in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]].

Past the hideout a slow underground river runs. It is an offshoot of the Fousan that either rejoins the river inside the city or runs on down into the earth, since no second river leaves Hallia. A makeshift dock beside the water was built to move beneath the city unseen, and a boat can be taken downriver from it.

The river leaves the sewers and runs into wild, unlit caves. It widens into a circular cavern about a hundred feet across, where a narrow three-foot ledge rings a central pit and the water plunges out of sight. The cave walls are craggy. On the far side of the pit a lift is built into the rock, and a two-hundred-foot ladder climbs from its platform to a heavy iron hatch that opens back into another stretch of the sewers. The platform is a staging area still in use, stocked with hard hats that carry lamps, flashlights, nutrition bars, food and water, and marked by no organization.

Below this the lift descends for about fifteen minutes in the dark to a cavern where purple crystals on the ceiling cast a bluish glow. Two giant serpents live in the pools there. They speak, and they let no one pass without knowing who they are and seeing a permission slip.

Closer to [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]] the sewers change. The newer tunnels are [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]]'s, laid in the last century; nearer the district's border they give way to the older works built by the Calarian royal family before it was deposed. Those tunnels have raised platforms on either side, so a body can walk clear of the flow, and no street grates, so they carry their own light. The walls are cobbled and catacomb-like and the refuse is thick in the air.

Where the tunnel opens out near the border there is a maintained sewage works, occupied and kept up though nobody is in sight. It looks like a parking lot: a staging area with stacked crates and one or two small boats tied along the water, enough flow that a shallow craft could pass. A shrine has been built around a machine that glows blue, and the machine does not touch the sewer around it. Oozes in disguise guarded it as puddles that moved when nobody was looking: [[Bestiary/Oozes|ochre jellies]], a [[Bestiary/Oozes|gray ooze]], and one thing of [[Bestiary/Oozes|living tar]]. They are dead now, and water on the ground is most of what is left of them.

The shrine stands at the center of the clearing. A seated figure of stone, about eight feet from where it sits to the top of its head, robed and androgynous, with two points where horns would be: the right straight and pointing up, the left cut off and sanded down to a flat stump. Tiny humanoids, each about an eighth of an inch tall and carved from the same stone, are spread across the floor around it and climbing its legs. Magic is gathered in the figure the way it gathers in a place where people have prayed, and nothing else in the shrine is magic. The figure matches no god or inner god [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] knows, and is not fiendish, demonic or devilish; he takes it for the work of some unrelated cult. Its magic vibrates in the same style as the tree at the [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] post office and the [[Phenomena/Radar Dishes|radar dishes]], though it oscillates differently.

The blue light in the machinery is not the machines giving off light. Behind glass, a glowing blue liquid runs through channels in them like veins, fast enough to see. In the pillars where it rises it is a darker blue that gives off little light; it reaches the top, something happens, and it comes back down glowing much brighter. Much of the machinery is pumps, gathering magic from somewhere above and carrying it below. The metal is an alloy of iron and lead, which holds magic in; without it the place would be a beacon. The blue is the same as in guns from [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]] and in the light one of the oozes threw.

Past the shrine the tunnel runs on into a straight hall sixty feet across, lined with the same pillars, with no end in sight. The sound of running water hangs at the edge of hearing and seems to grow louder and recede at once. The farther one walks the lighter one feels, and the rate at which one grows lighter picks up the longer the walk goes on; weight returns on the way back. About a mile in, roughly three quarters of the way through Teller's Run, there is a hairline crack in the air, like a fracture in a clear pane of glass, with the hall apparently running on beyond it. It gives off more magic than [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] has felt from anything, too much to be measured, and it looks like a smaller version of the crack in the [[Phenomena/Firmament|firmament]]. A hand brought within about six inches of it makes the world around seem to crack and the sight splinter, and both heal when the hand is pulled back. The crack does not open, and there is no space to pass through.

On the sewer side of the crack, the old stonework gave way to a recent metal construction: an antechamber hung with clear tarps and rubberized suits, and a cluttered room of desks and instruments with blue tubes along the walls. A box glowing green there was a terminal wired to a tape mainframe, the same system as the compound on the far side of the fracture, and it held the [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]]'s experiment results and personal logs. The station is destroyed. The hall it stood in caved in with it, and pipes broken open in the blast spill the blue liquid across the floor. The mainframe was the control system for the pumps that gather magic toward the crack; with it gone that system has stopped.
